  "notes": "lane/idxclient: the chat's field (GuiChat.initGui's) whole, over Java's UTF-16 text (gui_chat.c: the editing keys with shift and control, the word jumps with func_146183_a reading the cursor, the clipboard, the scroll that keeps the selection's end drawn, a click placing the cursor), drawn by raster_hud.c draw_text_box (the underscore and bar cursors, the selection's inversion). The other screens that make a GuiTextField (the anvil's, the sign's, the book's, the command block's, the server lists') are behind world.conf switches or outside single player. idx-chattype-s1, idx-chatsleep-s1 rows and play_check 0 mismatches; idx-chatdraw-s1 frames within 4 px."
